# Afenda external context (Context7 & MCP)

Stack versions and Context7 library hints: `.agents/stack-context.md`.

## Priority (framework APIs)

1. **Repo doctrine** — `docs/architecture/` (`ARCH-###`), `.cursor/rules/*`, session hooks routing
2. **Next.js 16** — **next-devtools** MCP `init` at session start for `apps/erp` work; then `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before generic Next docs (see root `AGENTS.md`)
3. **Context7** — add `use context7` for version-matched library APIs (Drizzle, Playwright, Tailwind v4, Vercel AI SDK, etc.)
4. **Web search** — only if Context7 has no library match

## MCP (global + project)

| Scope | Server | Use for |
| ----- | ------ | ------- |
| **Global** (`~/.cursor/mcp.json`) | **context7** | Third-party API docs — `CONTEXT7_API_KEY` recommended (§L or `mcp.json` `env`) |
| **Global** | **Neon** | DB — OAuth via **Connect** in Cursor MCP settings |
| **Global** | **github** | Remote MCP — **OAuth Connect** (preferred) or PAT via `GITHUB_TOKEN` + `env:sync:cursor` |
| **Global** | **vercel** | Deploys (OAuth in Cursor) |
| **Global** | **playwright** | Browser automation / E2E |
| **Project** (`.cursor/mcp.json`) | **shadcn** | `apps/erp/components.json` registry only |
| **Project** | **next-devtools** | Next.js 16+ app work — call **`init`** at session start (see `afenda-erp-app`) |

**Authority:** global MCP is operator-owned (shared across Afenda repos); this repo does not ship a full project MCP manifest. Env: `.env.config` §L → `pnpm env:sync:cursor` (Windows User env for MCP keys). App env: `pnpm env:sync` only. Details and troubleshooting: `docs/development/env.md`. Skill: `context7-mcp`.

TypeScript: `packages/config/tsconfig.base.json` (`strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, unused-symbol checks). Vercel link deferred until ARCH-001 stabilization gate passes.

## Do not use Context7 for

- Tenancy, capabilities, org resolution (**ARCH-001**, `@afenda/auth`)
- Governed list authority, metadata vs runtime (**ARCH-006**, **ARCH-007**)
- Package boundaries, export doors, and imports (**ARCH-008**, **ARCH-002**, **ARCH-003**)
- Afenda-specific shadcn paths — components live in `packages/ui`; use shadcn MCP from ERP `components.json` aliases
